  <outputs>
    <file>src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/services/sendEmailService.ts</file>
    <file>src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/services/openRecordLauncher.ts</file>
  </outputs>

  <notes>
    **Completed 2026-10-02**, executed as a background Sonnet-5 subagent in the shared worktree
    (parallel with the main session's task 076; office-addins-only, no git state changes). Client-only —
    no BFF file touched.

    `openRecordLauncher.buildOpenRecordUrl` now appends `navbar=off` unconditionally (never `cmdbar=false`)
    — one change, consumed by `SaveFlow.tsx`'s Open affordances AND `sendEmailService.ts`'s record link.
    Added generic `openUrlInBrowserWindow` (reuses the existing `defaultOpener`) for the Word choice to
    open through, not a second mechanism.

    `sendEmailService.ts`: extracted the existing link-resolution step (document share-link mint + record
    deep link) into a shared `resolveSendEmailLinks`, used by BOTH the unchanged Outlook path
    (`prepareSendEmail`) and the new `prepareWordSendEmailChoice` — structurally enforces "never mint a
    link a second way," not just by convention. Added `buildSpaarkeComposeUrl` (the
    `sprk_communicationpage` `data=` envelope, verified against `parseParams.ts`/`index.tsx`, HTML body),
    `buildOutlookWebComposeUrl` (the documented `outlook.office.com` deep link, plain-text body), and
    `resolveSendEmailAffordance` (the one pure, tested gating function: `'outlook-native' | 'word-choice' |
    'none'`, capability-only per NFR-10).

    **A real encoding bug was found and fixed during this task's own verification**: the first
    `buildSpaarkeComposeUrl` used a single-encode construction that is silently corrupted by
    `parseParams.ts`'s real (unconditional, double) decode sequence whenever a field value contains a
    literal `&amp;`/`=` — exactly what the embedded four-param record URL and an "X &amp; Y"-style subject both
    are. Caught by a round-trip test reproducing the REAL decode algorithm (not the test's own encoding
    assumptions); fixed via explicit `encodeURIComponent(inner.toString())`. Full derivation in
    `notes/086-word-send-email-and-focused-open.md`.

    `App.tsx`: extracted `buildSendEmailRelatedRecordInput` (shared by both Send Email paths); added
    `handleSendEmailChoice`; replaced the single `canSendEmail` boolean with the `resolveSendEmailAffordance`
    result, rendering the unchanged single Button for Outlook or a new Fluent v9 `Menu` (two `MenuItem`s —
    "Spaarke email" / "Outlook on the web") for Word; neither renders when there is nothing to link or
    neither capability holds.

    Deviation: the POML's `&lt;relevant-files&gt;` named `SaveFlow.tsx` as a Send Email edit target; the
    affordance actually lives in `App.tsx` (confirmed by grep before writing anything) — `SaveFlow.tsx` was
    not touched. Gating is tested via the extracted pure `resolveSendEmailAffordance` rather than mounting
    the full `App.tsx` in RTL (no precedent for that in this package; task 036 took the same proportionate
    approach for the Outlook button).

    Neither escalation trigger fired: the Communication page's compose-mode pre-fill works from a plain
    browser URL (verified by reading `index.tsx`/`parseParams.ts`/`App.tsx`). CORRECTED on main-session review:
    it does NOT match `createTodoLauncher.ts` — that launcher appends flat params to a configured base URL, not
    `main.aspx?...&amp;data=`; the `data=` form has no shipped precedent here, so the live check is its first proof); the Outlook-web body-length trigger was not
    measured live (no live host reachable here) but is not expected to fire given the body's actual length
    — recorded as an estimate, not a verification.

    Gates: gated jest 62/62 suites, 836/836 tests (817 before this task's +19 new tests — no new suite
    file; both touched test files were already gated from tasks 027/036); lint exit 0; `npm run typecheck`
    68 total / **0 production** (pinned baseline, after fixing one `exactOptionalPropertyTypes` regression
    introduced and caught mid-task); `npm run build` exit 0. Self-run code-review + adr-check: 0 Critical,
    0 Warning, 1 Suggestion (a minor naming nit); 0 ADR violations.

    Acceptance criterion 8 (live, post-deploy check) left open — no deployed SWA / live Office host /
    Dataverse session reachable from this environment. Full report: `notes/086-word-send-email-and-focused-open.md`.
  </notes>

